From db8b8d4130457dbe46558a7cea872dd2dae539e6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Navid Ghahremani <ghahramani.navid@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 18:13:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] sanechips: add support for ZTE ZXHN H3600

Add the H3600 board description, flash layout, sysupgrade support and
OpenWrt LED, calibration and network setup. Use per-unit Wi-Fi addresses
and kernel color/function LED names.

Validate H3600 archive format, board directory, and uImage headers before
flashing, retaining generic metadata checks and UBI layout guards.

Hardware specification:
- SoC: Sanechips ZX279128S, two ARM Cortex-A9 cores with PL310 L2 cache
- RAM: 512 MiB DDR3
- Flash: 128 MiB HeYangTek HYF1GQ4UDACAE SPI NAND
- Wi-Fi: MediaTek MT7915D, 2.4/5 GHz 802.11ax, 2T2R/4T4R, dual PCIe
- Ethernet: four Gigabit LAN ports and one Gigabit WAN port, SoC switch
- LEDs/buttons: 11 GPIO LED outputs (including bicolor power/internet),
  four buttons (reset, WPS, Wi-Fi and LED toggle)
- UART: X1A22, 3.3 V TTL, 115200 8N1; pins 1=VCC, 2=TX, 3=RX, 4=GND
- Power: 12 V DC, 1.5 A

Flash instructions:
1. Connect a 3.3 V serial adapter to X1A22 (cross TX/RX; leave VCC open).
   Connect the TFTP server to LAN1 at 192.168.1.2/24, with WAN unplugged.
2. Serve openwrt-sanechips-generic-zte_zxhn-h3600-initramfs.uImage.
3. Press 1 once at cspboot's boot-mode prompt, enter the unit's boot-mode
   password, and run these commands at the U-Boot prompt:
     setenv ipaddr 192.168.1.1
     setenv serverip 192.168.1.2
     tftp 0x43000000 openwrt-sanechips-generic-zte_zxhn-h3600-initramfs.uImage
     bootm 0x43000000
4. Back up the bootloader, factory data and stock slot from the RAM system.
   Copy the matching squashfs-sysupgrade.bin to /tmp and install with:
     sysupgrade -n /tmp/openwrt-sanechips-generic-zte_zxhn-h3600-squashfs-sysupgrade.bin

The raw kernel is 4 MiB. UBI occupies 57 MiB beyond both firmware slots,
so the vendor header scanner sees both slot headers before UBI.

Reverting to stock:
The stock slot at 0x2700000..0x4700000 is preserved read-only. Retain the
unit's original backups and use its vendor boot/recovery procedure to
return to stock.

MAC address layout:
- LAN1-LAN4: tag partition, binary factory base at offset 0x1e
- WAN: factory base + 1, provided by the mac-base NVMEM cell
- 2.4 GHz: factory base + 2 with the locally administered bit set
- 5 GHz: factory base + 3 with the locally administered bit set
The Wi-Fi hotplug hook updates the wiphy address before interface setup;
OpenWrt allocates individual SSID addresses. Factory radio calibration
comes from wifi partition's JFFS2 file caldata and remains unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Navid Ghahremani <ghahramani.navid@gmail.com>
